    {
      "number": 541,
      "title": "trust: secret redaction, token encryption, and Sendable safety",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```rust\n// Provider tokens are now encrypted at rest\nlet store = PostgresStore::new(config).await?;\nstore.save_provider_token(\"github\", &token).await?; // encrypted via AES-256-GCM\n\n// Secrets are redacted in logs and agent output\ntracing::info!(\"token: {}\", secret.redacted()); // \"token: [REDACTED]\"\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nHardens lfd's trust paths: provider tokens stored in SQLite/Postgres are now encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM with keys stored in the OS keychain (macOS Keychain, Linux secret-tool, or a file fallback). Secret values are redacted in logs. Swift services gain `@unchecked Sendable` annotations with safety documentation. Wave trust roadmap updated to mark sprints 01–03 as shipped.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Token encryption** — new `token_crypto` module with AES-256-GCM encrypt/decrypt, key derivation via OS keychain or file fallback, and automatic migration of plaintext tokens on startup\n- **Secret redaction** — `LFD_ENCRYPTION_KEY` and sensitive config fields are masked in logs and registration output\n- **Sendable safety** — Swift service types annotated with `@unchecked Sendable` and `// SAFETY:` comments documenting thread-safety invariants\n- **Postgres migration atomicity** — token migration now runs in a transaction\n- **Key storage cleanup** — removed trailing newlines from stored encryption keys\n- **Docker hardening** — install script and Dockerfile updated for encryption dependencies\n- **Wave roadmap** — trust sprints 01–03 marked complete, remaining items consolidated",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 989,
      "deletions": 216,
      "changed_files": 38
    },
    {
      "number": 542,
      "title": "flow: execute ops items directly and hand off judgment via scratch",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```yaml\n# ship-roadmap flow — land is now a direct ops call, not an agent session\n- ingest\n- kickoff\n- review-design\n- build\n- review\n- ops: land --create-pr\n```\n\n```bash\n# gate writes PR copy that land consumes automatically\nlf gate                    # → scratch/pr-title.txt, scratch/pr-body.md, scratch/.pr-copy-ref\nlf ops land --create-pr    # reads cached copy, no --title/--body needed\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds `ops:` as a first-class flow item type. Flows can now execute mechanical operations (land, rebase, release) directly via Rust functions — no agent session startup cost. Gate writes PR copy files to scratch/ for handoff. Land reads them, validates freshness via SHA check, and clears scratch/ after consuming. Release notes are now narrative via a `release-notes` step invoked as a subprocess.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `FlowItem::Ops(OpsItem)` variant with YAML parsing, expansion, and execution in both CLI and daemon flow runners\n- `gate` step extended to write `scratch/pr-title.txt` + `scratch/pr-body.md` + `scratch/.pr-copy-ref`\n- `lf ops land` reads cached PR copy, validates against HEAD SHA, falls back to CLI args\n- `release_run` invokes `lf release-notes` subprocess for narrative notes\n- New `release-notes` builtin step\n- Python `FlowStep.from_raw()` handles ops items; Swift `FlowProgressPills` renders with distinct styling\n- Updated `ship-roadmap`, `ship`, `release` flows to use `ops:` items\n- Tests: flow parsing, land cached PR copy, release tag idempotency",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 940,
      "deletions": 83,
      "changed_files": 27
    },
    {
      "number": 543,
      "title": "config: remove unused fields, clean stale artifacts, separate repo/user init guidance",
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- **Remove `push` and `include_loopflow_doc` config fields** — parsed but never wired up. `push` was handled by `lf ops commit -p`; `include_loopflow_doc` had no consumers. Removed from `Config` struct, `Default` impl, and tests.\n- **Update init step to separate repo vs user config** — the builtin `init.md` now checks for `~/.lf/config.yaml`, distinguishes repo config (agent, harnesses, exclude) from user config (yolo, ide, chrome), and offers to create user config if missing. No longer scaffolds `yolo: false` or `push: false` into repo config.\n- **Improve agent error message** — use `durable_log_dir()` for the log path hint instead of hardcoding `~/.lf/logs/`.\n- **Delete ~13,000 lines of stale artifacts** — `.agents/skills/` (superseded by builtin steps), `proto/` (unused protobuf definitions), `reports/` (old research docs), `bin/` scripts, and symlinks.\n- **Remove `push` from docs and goldens** — updated `docs/config.md`, bundled `LOOPFLOW.md` config example, `.lf/config.yaml`, and all 7 golden test files.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ncargo test --all                  # all Rust tests pass\ncargo clippy -- -D warnings       # clean\ncargo fmt --check                 # formatted\n```\n\nExisting repo configs with `push:` or `include_loopflow_doc:` silently ignore the unknown fields (no `deny_unknown_fields`), so no migration needed.",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 94,
      "deletions": 13564,
      "changed_files": 147
    },
    {
      "number": 544,
      "title": "lf land: auto-generate PR copy and improve worktree rotation",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\n# land now generates PR title/body automatically if not provided\nlf ops land\n\n# pr create/update also auto-generates when --title is omitted\nlf ops pr\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n`lf ops land` and `lf ops pr` now auto-generate PR title and body via the Claude API when not explicitly provided. Previously both commands required `--title` and `--body` flags. The generation uses the diff against the base branch to produce structured PR copy.\n\nWorktree creation now syncs the default branch from origin before branching, and worktree rotation during land uses the branch's own timestamp for the preserved directory name instead of the current time.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `lf ops pr` `--title`/`--body` are now optional; omitting them triggers LLM-based generation from the diff\n- `lf ops land` generates PR copy after rebase (so the diff is final) and falls back to LLM generation when no cached gate output exists\n- Cached PR copy validation tightened: only accepted if HEAD is at most 1 commit ahead of the cached ref, not just any ancestor\n- `create_with_schema_synced` variant syncs origin/main before creating worktrees\n- `preserve_worktree` accepts an optional suffix, used to name archived worktrees by their branch timestamp\n- Worktree rotation pushes the new branch synchronously instead of via background thread\n- Shell directive comment updated to mention `lf ops land` alongside other cd-emitting commands\n- Squash-merged detection in `list_worktrees_local` now also requires `has_commits` to avoid false positives",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 565,
      "deletions": 91,
      "changed_files": 12
    },
    {
      "number": 545,
      "title": "release: v0.9.8",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nBump version to 0.9.8 across all manifests and update release notes.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Version bump from 0.9.7 → 0.9.8 in `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `pyproject.toml`, and `uv.lock`\n- Rewritten `RELEASE_NOTES.md` covering: first-class `ops:` flow items, token encryption at rest, session context UI, ~13k lines of stale artifact cleanup, and worktree rotation improvements",
