    {
      "number": 546,
      "title": "ops: auto-recover from rebase conflicts with agent fallback",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf ops rebase          # auto-launches agent on conflict\nlf ops land            # recovers from rebase conflict, retries land\nlf ops pr              # recovers from rebase conflict, retries PR\nlf wt prune            # prunes merged worktrees (no --force needed)\nlf wt prune --include-fresh  # also prune worktrees with no commits\n```\n\nWhen `rebase`, `land`, or `pr` hit a rebase conflict, they now launch a step agent to resolve it instead of failing. The agent gets the conflict context via `<lf:rebase-conflict>` and uses the rebase step to fix things up, then the original command retries.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New `RebaseConflict` error variant in `OpsError` — rebase returns structured conflict info instead of a generic error\n- `launch_step_agent` function runs a named step headlessly when ops commands need agent judgment\n- Rebase step docs simplified: removed fast-path concept, focused on conflict resolution\n- Worktree pruning reworked: new `fresh` field tracks worktrees with no commits beyond main, `--force` replaced by `--include-fresh`, merged worktrees prune without confirmation\n- Removed `git2` crate dependency (replaced by git CLI calls)\n- `land` now stages uncommitted changes before proceeding\n- Added `diff_names` helper for listing changed files between commits\n- Install script improvements for binary resolution",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 387,
      "deletions": 258,
      "changed_files": 14
    },
    {
