    },
    {
      "number": 553,
      "title": "lf commit: auto-generate commit messages via agent",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\n# Commit with auto-generated message (no -m required)\nlf commit\n\n# Still works with explicit message\nlf commit -m \"manual message\"\n```\n\n`lf commit` no longer requires an explicit message. When no message is provided, it generates one by sending the staged diff to a lightweight agent (claude:haiku) with a builtin prompt, then formats the result as `lf <task>: <generated title>`.\n\nThis also applies to internal auto-commit paths — `auto_commit_if_dirty` and `post_step_sync` now go through the same `commit_workflow` codepath instead of calling raw git helpers directly.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `commit_workflow` generates a commit message via agent when none is provided, falling back to a prefix-only message if generation fails\n- New helpers: `generate_commit_message`, `format_commit_message`, `parse_commit_message`, `staged_diff`, `truncate_chars`\n- `auto_commit_if_dirty` and `post_step_sync` now use `CommitOptions` + `commit_workflow` instead of manual `stage_all`/`commit` calls\n- Codex agent command always passes `--json` when streaming (removes `stream_format` guard)\n- Tests updated: `commit_requires_message` → `commit_generates_message_when_none`",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 165,
      "deletions": 29,
      "changed_files": 4
    },
    {
      "number": 554,
      "title": "release: v0.9.9",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf ops release run patch\n```\n\nBumps version to 0.9.9 across all manifests and updates release notes.\n\n## Summary\n\nRelease v0.9.9 introduces auto-generated commit messages via a lightweight agent and adds a fail-fast check when a release tag already exists on origin.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Version bump to 0.9.9 in `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `pyproject.toml`, and `uv.lock`\n- Updated `RELEASE_NOTES.md` with v0.9.9 notes covering `lf commit` auto-generation and release tag collision detection",
